  "version": 134,
  "method": "Built-in image_gen; two continuous atlas references and 30 original regional paintings. Original complete plaza retained. Overview uses runtime feather weights.",
  "promptTemplate": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Production terrain tile for Hyper Dimension. The attached {bounds.w}x{bounds.h} crop is the exact composition target for tile ({col},{row}) of a unified island map. Repaint at high native resolution, ideally {bounds.w*3}x{bounds.h*3}, EXACT aspect {bounds.w}:{bounds.h}. {themeStyle}: crisp pixel clusters for pixel, layered paper folds for origami. Preserve the reference's exact geometry and palette: every green building parcel, plaza ring/star, farm bed, road, waterfall, mine, coast, rock, tree silhouette and all edge intersections stay fixed. Increase fine detail without changing layout. ALL four edges must continue at the precise original coordinates and angles because neighboring crops share the same master. No zoom/reframe/shift, no perspective change, no extra features, no additional clearings. Neutral daylight only. Terrain only: NO houses (the existing farm utility shed and mine structure may remain exactly where shown), no people, UI, text, watermarks or borders. The gallery district and mainland are continuous solid land, no added bridge, dock or isolated island. Roads stay open and meet logically. Full bleed, no seam lines or darkened perimeter. For the plaza, the complete star and paving keep their geometry even where cropped; do not invent a new star center. High-quality original fine painting, not blurred or merely scaled reference.",
